{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1257504-information-on-prussia-and-baltic-in-c-td","id":1257504,"title":"Information on Prussia and Baltic in C:tD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-09-26T23:34:57-07:00","id":1257504,"title":"Information on Prussia and Baltic in C:tD","content":"If anyone have a copy of Trolle, Tr\u00e4umer, Tiefe W\u00e4lder \u2014 are there any information on fae history in Prussia? And are there, generally, any canon information on changelings in the Baltic, beyond the name of Pomeranian Alliance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6231-mindszenty","name":"mindszenty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-28T12:51:52-07:00","id":1257821,"title":"","content":"I can't say its canon, but I have an NPC Autumn Sidhe who was strongly effected by her history in first the Commonwealth, and then Prussia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-11T01:43:56-07:00","id":1260091,"title":"","content":"They sort of got some of the Geography wrong and called parts of Poland parts of Germany instead on that one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3988-windthin","name":"Windthin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3988_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-11T11:41:38-07:00","id":1260168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Windthin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1257504-information-on-prussia-and-baltic-in-c-td?p=1260091#post1260091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They sort of got some of the Geography wrong and called parts of Poland parts of Germany instead on that one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't Modern Poland cover parts of Historic Prussia?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-14T14:52:03-07:00","id":1260572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1257504-information-on-prussia-and-baltic-in-c-td?p=1260168#post1260168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Doesn't Modern Poland cover parts of Historic Prussia?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. To replace the vast area of Poland that Stalin gave Russia, Poland got Prussia. Prussia wasn't German until fairly late. The locals were Balts like the Lithuanians. The Teutonic Knight hunted the local pagans for sport mainly. Long after the Prussian people became Christian the Teutonic Knights hunted them for sport and allowed paying guests, who got credit for going on Crusade.<br /> <br /> The local Dreaming would be distinctive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T20:19:38-07:00","id":1296877,"title":"","content":"I checked, however, I looked closely at maps and the areas they delineated definitely were not where they stated them to be. They kind of muddled up the coastal regions in western Poland and eastern Germany.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3988-windthin","name":"Windthin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3988_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}